\\" Chuck Bednarik, a legendary linebacker and center for the Philadelphia Eagles, died at the age of 89 following a brief illness. During his 14-season career with the Eagles, Bednarik played on two NFL championship teams and was inducted into the Pro Football Hall of Fame in 1967. He is best known for his performance in the 1960 NFL championship game against the Green Packers, where he made a tackle as time ran out to preserve an victory. 
